# REQUIRES: cuda, python-api, torch, parmed
# The derivative in the positions through mdir.torch with the extra points
# of Amber (D385, D384, #771), on a GPU: OPC from a
# prmtop cut by ParmEd (with the interpreter of the tests, which has it),
# the gradient in theta alone given with positions that require a
# gradient, against FrameEnergies.vjp, and the forms that take the
# positions refused, naming the extra points.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_sites.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide cut GPU Double %t
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_hvp_torch.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide amber GPU Double %t | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Double torch"
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_frame_hvp_torch.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide amber GPU Mixed %t | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Mixed torch"

# CHECK: [[MODE]]: Amber OPC (ACE-ALA-NME and 40 waters), 2 frames: grad(L, theta) and L.backward(inputs=theta), with positions that require a gradient, against FrameEnergies.vjp, to the bit; grad(L, x), grad(L, [theta, x]), and L.backward() refused, naming virtual sites placed by the directions of their bonds
